      <ExpenseAmt>196149</ExpenseAmt>
      <Desc>A vendored program with the San Diego Regional Center (SDRC) that provides individualized, person-centered support to adults with disabilities. Services are customized to each participants goals and may include community integration, employment preparation, educational enrichment, and life-skills development.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>90291</ExpenseAmt>
        <Desc>A vendored program with the San Diego Regional Center (SDRC) that empowers adults with disabilities to develop and manage their own micro-businesses. Participants receive hands-on instruction and individualized support in areas such as business planning, marketing, financial literacy, and operations. Program costs are funded directly by the SDRC as part of its mission to promote independence and vocational growth for individuals with developmental disabilities.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>24907</ExpenseAmt>
        <Desc>This program provides inclusive educational opportunities for adults with disabilities by allowing participants to use their authorized disability service funds to attend classes offered through our organization. Funding is administered by a third-party Fiscal Management Service (FMS) on behalf of the Regional Center system, which oversees disability service programs statewide. Through this model, individuals can engage in creative, skill-building, and community-based learning experiences that promote personal growth and independence.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
